{"mix":{"enabled":true,"tuning":{"half_life_days":14.0,"familiar":6.0,"curve":2.0,"floor":0.0,"rest_hours":24.0,"new_days":0.0,"new_boost":2.0,"window":30.0,"again":0.25,"tired":0.25,"unsorted":1.0},"categories":[{"key":"transit","name":"Trains & transit","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Getting around on the ground: railways, subways, buses, streetcars, monorails, commuter rail, transit agencies and their PSAs (Amtrak, VIA, TTC, STCUM, BART, Metro, Eurostar, Shinkansen, Greyhound). Includes rail memes like Third Rail Thursday only if it is mostly real trains. A transit agency or railway selling the ride stays here even when the destination is the hook (a World's Fair, an airport, a ballpark). Oil-company sponsors go to energy."},{"key":"travel","name":"Air travel & places","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Airlines, airplanes and Concorde, and selling a place: tourism boards, world's fairs and Expos, theme parks, aquariums (Air Canada, TWA, British Airways, Boeing, Bonjour Québec, Expo 86, Hersheypark)."},{"key":"tech","name":"Phones & computers","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Telephone companies and long distance, computers, software, the internet, fax machines, modems, VCRs, Walkmans and other electronics, and big tech corporate image spots (Bell, AT&T, Northern Telecom, IBM, Apple, Microsoft, Commodore, Cox, TiVo, Panasonic, Sony). Electronics and battery spots stay here even with an animal or a robot on screen."},{"key":"shopping","name":"Shops, food & cars","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Everyday consumer brands: grocery and retail stores, restaurants, food and drink, cars, banks, ATMs and credit cards, newspapers and magazines (Giant Food, A&P, Safeway, Zellers, Pizza Hut, Doritos, McDonald's, Starbucks, Chrysler, VW, BMO, Visa, Wall Street Journal). National brands only (local ones go to local). A store, car, bank or newspaper ad stays here even when it pitches inflation or fuel economy."},{"key":"local","name":"Local & regional","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Someone's local ad: one city's or region's businesses and institutions, from anywhere. Malls and outlet centres, local and regional stores and grocery chains (Giant Food), local newspapers (Washington Post, Baltimore Sun, City Paper, Montreal Gazette), local TV stations and their promos (WMAR, WETA), local teams' promos, city pride promos (Lansing), regional companies (DuPont). Local wins over what it sells, except transit, which stays in transit."},{"key":"energy","name":"Energy & the 70s crisis","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Energy: conservation PSAs, fuel saving, inflation and 'buy American' economy messages of the 1970s-80s energy crisis, oil companies, electric and gas utilities, hydro, solar, nuclear, and heavy industry image ads (Burt Reynolds DOE, Gregory Peck, Johnny Cash Amoco, Petro-Canada, Chevron, Ontario Hydro, Hydro-Québec, Monsanto, DuPont). Also 1970s economy, productivity and buy-American messages and union-label ads."},{"key":"civic","name":"PSAs, politics & faith","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Public service and civic messages not about energy: government campaigns (metric system, census, civil defense, litter, 55 mph, new money and coins, digital TV), election and campaign ads (Mondale, real party ads), news clips, and religious spots (the LDS ads). A vox-pop that sells nothing is civic."},{"key":"tv","name":"TV & sports","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Television about television and sports: network and station promos and launches (HBO, ESPN, CNN, CBC, PBS, WETA, local news), sports teams and broadcasts (Expos, Orioles, Big Ten, Olympics), state media and anthem videos. National networks; a local station's promos go to local. PSAs about television itself stay here."},{"key":"cats","name":"Cats & animals","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Real animal footage where the animal is the point: cat clips and cat memes (the PunchingCat series, catslop the serval, manul, Keyboard Cat), puppies, wolves, pigeons, and vintage pet food ads that star the animal (Morris, Meow Mix). The PunchingCat series is always cats. A real animal clip counts even with a caption, an OS-window frame or a cutout; an AI-generated animal goes to slop."},{"key":"slop","name":"AI slop & memes","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"Internet stuff: AI diffusion video (Sora/Veo/minimax/gemini style: photoreal-ish people or animals that morph and warp) used for parody ads (A1 steak sauce, Canine.Cloud, Liberty Biberty, Draft Queens, corn train, the tuna cat, SlopHQ and sl parody political ads), AI voice dubs (the Seinfeld ones), and internet memes and brainrot that are not mainly animal clips (Never Give Up, Homer, Third Rail Thursday if it reads as a meme)."},{"key":"house","name":"Made here","weight":1.0,"wear":1.0,"about":"VizelVision's own pieces, made by Vivian and Hazel as code-rendered animation (clean 3D or vector shapes that hold steady, not diffusion video): how-it-works, Football Sunday, both PLQ vote cat PSAs, and probably the decimal time cat and 'us' (painterly two cats). Station-made explainers and announcements."}],"ads":{"8d00e900e77e":"tv","6a87aec1c2f2":"civic","c20998c3f709":"travel","09010fddc155":"local","9ab0d331a727":"transit","a00becbcc945":"transit","7d1b804ca017":"house","40fd1a39dacf":"tech","beb7ebc57b19":"house","74ccf7c35d05":"cats","27a820adbe93":"travel","2e107fd01429":"slop","83681a4dc129":"shopping","4ef129c26e3a":"house","cb2b94c6a165":"civic","da795f24d111":"house","5c7d30b7e1c9":"slop","348910a560e1":"local","749dbbcac7b2":"energy","30537ee2139b":"cats","320346dccfd6":"tech","bcdcc53d7c44":"shopping","84bb8946630c":"cats","bca380e3082b":"cats","93ac7dd42be0":"slop","5354e586da37":"travel","c43184194c50":"transit","140af476a748":"slop","156acf9651fe":"local","e9a7980b893b":"tech","6c91d4fc9c62":"civic","90cd9423bc8e":"shopping","5dcdd849fd5c":"energy","1262bcfafb48":"energy","2147a7c45f09":"tv","b9d4b47dbd49":"tv"},"overrides":{}},"now":1790907400.0,"order":"shuffle","summary":{"enabled":true,"aire